From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000248 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: fix calibrated provider PPM source context

The PPM source adapter's generated owner callbacks receive a
struct mt6797_dvfsp_ppm_source context. The calibrated-provider binding was
passing its enclosing provider instead, so the first lock or snapshot call
could not reach the validated source contract. Pass the embedded source and
exercise the callback context in the hardware-free provider test.

This changes no hardware or registration behavior.

---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider.c      | 2 +-
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider-test.c | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider.c
@@ -192,7 +192,7 @@ int mt6797_dvfsp_calibrated_provider_bind_sources(
 	ret = mt6797_dvfsp_calibrated_provider_init(provider, resource_owner,
 			&provider->bound_source_ops, provider,
-			&provider->bound_ppm_ops, provider,
+			&provider->bound_ppm_ops, &provider->ppm_source,
 			owner_handle, transition_handle);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider-test.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider-test.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider-test.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-calibrated-provider-test.c
@@ -252,6 +252,10 @@ static void mt6797_dvfsp_provider_binds_and_exits(
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, !!owner_ops.snapshot);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_TRUE(test, !!owner_ops.hold);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test,
+		provider.source.ppm_owner_ops->lock(
+			provider.source.ppm_owner_context), -EOPNOTSUPP);
+	KUNIT_EXPECT_PTR_EQ(test, provider.source.ppm_owner_context,
+			&provider.ppm_source);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test,
 		mt6797_dvfsp_calibrated_provider_exit(&provider), 0);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_FALSE(test, owner.source_bound);
 	KUNIT_EXPECT_EQ(test, mt6797_dvfsp_resource_owner_detach(&owner), 0);
